IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `coroners-dates`
IMPORT `coroners-owner`

-- Coroners Act 1997 (ACT) -- worked cases, from the seat of the owner or occupier of property.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Expected values were written by hand
-- from the deposited text (A1997-57, R51), never copied from the encoding's output. The facts are the encoder's,
-- HYPOTHETICAL throughout. Every opinion or satisfaction of an official is given as a fact.

GIVEN d IS A NUMBER, m IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`on` d m y MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY d m y

§ `s 18 -- an inquiry into the fire`

-- Arguments: the Attorney-General asked, I asked, the coroner considers an inquiry should be held.
#ASSERT `Must there be an inquiry into the fire question` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: the Attorney-General has asked, so a coroner must hold an inquiry into the cause and origin of the fire (s 18(1))`
#ASSERT `Must there be an inquiry into the fire question` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `yes: the Attorney-General has asked, so a coroner must hold an inquiry into the cause and origin of the fire (s 18(1))`
-- A house destroyed in a fire of unknown origin; the owner asks and the coroner agrees one should be held.
#ASSERT `Must there be an inquiry into the fire question` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `possibly: the coroner considers an inquiry should be held, and may hold one at my request or on the coroner's own initiative (s 18(2)); it is a discretion`
#ASSERT `Must there be an inquiry into the fire question` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `possibly: the coroner considers an inquiry should be held, and may hold one at my request or on the coroner's own initiative (s 18(2)); it is a discretion`
#ASSERT `Must there be an inquiry into the fire question` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no: the coroner is of the opinion that no inquiry should be held, and must give me written notice of that opinion and its grounds (s 18(3))`
#ASSERT `Must there be an inquiry into the fire question` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not unless the Attorney-General asks or the coroner considers an inquiry should be held; as owner or occupier I may ask for one (s 18(2))`

§ `s 54(2) -- the fire findings`

#ASSERT `Can I get a copy of the fire findings question` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `yes: I have asked, and the coroner must make a copy of the findings available to me as owner (s 54(2))`
#ASSERT `Can I get a copy of the fire findings question` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `yes, if I ask: on my request as owner the coroner must make a copy of the findings available to me (s 54(2))`
-- A tenant whose belongings burned: an occupier, not the owner.
#ASSERT `Can I get a copy of the fire findings question` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `not covered: s 54(2) gives a copy to the owner of the property; an occupier who is not the owner is not named`

§ `s 66 -- search warrants`

#ASSERT `Must I be given a copy of the warrant question` TRUE EQUALS `yes: before exercising any power under the warrant, the person executing it must give me, as owner or occupier, a copy of it (s 66(6))`
#ASSERT `Must I be given a copy of the warrant question` FALSE EQUALS `the person executing the warrant has not done what s 66(6) requires: a copy must be given to the owner or occupier before any power under it is exercised`

-- A warrant issued 31 January 2027: 1 month later is 28 February 2027 (no 31 February).
#ASSERT `Is the warrant in force question` (`on` 31 1 2027) (`on` 28 2 2027) (`on` 28 2 2027) EQUALS `yes: the day is within the period from the date of issue to the end of the date stated in the warrant (s 66(5))`
#ASSERT `Is the warrant in force question` (`on` 31 1 2027) (`on` 28 2 2027) (`on` 31 1 2027) EQUALS `yes: the day is within the period from the date of issue to the end of the date stated in the warrant (s 66(5))`
#ASSERT `Is the warrant in force question` (`on` 31 1 2027) (`on` 28 2 2027) (`on` 1 3 2027) EQUALS `no: the warrant has ceased to have effect at the end of the date stated in it (s 66(4)(d), (5))`
#ASSERT `Is the warrant in force question` (`on` 31 1 2027) (`on` 28 2 2027) (`on` 30 1 2027) EQUALS `no: the warrant could not yet be executed, as the day is before its date of issue (s 66(5))`
#ASSERT `Is the warrant in force question` (`on` 31 1 2027) (`on` 1 3 2027) (`on` 15 2 2027) EQUALS `the warrant does not meet s 66(4)(d): the date it states for ceasing to have effect is more than 1 month after its date of issue`

§ `Part 5A -- coronial investigation scenes`

-- An order made 1 January 2027 may end no later than 31 January 2027.
#ASSERT `Is the scene order end date lawful question` (`on` 1 1 2027) (`on` 31 1 2027) EQUALS `the order's end date is within the limit: no later than 30 days after the order was made (s 68C(2)(b)(ii))`
#ASSERT `Is the scene order end date lawful question` (`on` 1 1 2027) (`on` 1 2 2027) EQUALS `the order does not meet s 68C(2)(b)(ii): its end date is more than 30 days after the order was made`

-- A current order ending 31 January 2027: an extension may run to 2 March 2027 (February 2027 has 28 days).
#ASSERT `Latest end of a scene extension question` (`on` 31 1 2027) TRUE TRUE EQUALS `an extension may run to` (`on` 2 3 2027)
#ASSERT `Latest end of a scene extension question` (`on` 31 1 2027) FALSE TRUE EQUALS `no extension: the coroner may extend the order only if satisfied that an extension is in the interests of justice (s 68C(3)(b))`
#ASSERT `Latest end of a scene extension question` (`on` 31 1 2027) TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no extension: an extension must be ordered before the current order ends (s 68C(3))`

-- A senior police officer's declaration: 23 hours on; exactly 24 hours on; 2 hours on, with a coroner's order since.
#ASSERT `Is the police scene declaration in force question` 23 FALSE EQUALS `the declaration is in force, for at most 24 hours from when it was made (s 68F(3)(b)(ii))`
#ASSERT `Is the police scene declaration in force question` 24 FALSE EQUALS `the declaration has ended: 24 hours have passed since it was made (s 68F(3)(b)(ii))`
#ASSERT `Is the police scene declaration in force question` 2 TRUE EQUALS `the declaration has ended: a coronial investigation scene order has been issued for the place (s 68F(3)(b)(i)); the order now governs`
